xt{", "MATHSEG_0002": "}\\mathfrak q\n\\Leftrightarrow\n\\mathfrak pS_{\\mathfrak q} = \\mathfrak q S_{\\mathfrak q}\n\\text{", "MATHSEG_0003": "}\n\\kappa(\\mathfrak p) \\subset \\kappa(\\mathfrak q)\\text{", "MATHSEG_0004": "}\n$$", "MATH_0001": "$R \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Omega_{S/R} = 0$", "MATH_0003": "$R \\to S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathfrak q \\subset S$", "MATH_0005": "$g \\in S$", "MATH_0006": "$g \\not \\in \\mathfrak q$", "MATH_0007": "$R \\to S_g$", "MATH_0008": "$R \\to S$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathfrak q$", "MATH_0010": "$S$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathfrak p \\subset R$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-section-unramified}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-unramified-at-prime}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-characterize-unramified}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:057aedd6438329ab70bf05e6cab30f33b8628d2386e283a7d7873cf61303e627", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:acfdef3ca6d29c15ddb84e6f619ffadfa1875d32402b26fe6445ba35e744dfcc", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e5c51e4c293ddf106dcc15d60706688ff4c7c9bb19acc7ba97cf6116a5184348", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis is the local version of the\ndefinition in Algebra, Section <REF_0001>.\nIn that section a ring map <MATH_0001> is defined to be unramified if and\nonly if it is of finite type, and <MATH_0002>.\nWe say <MATH_0003> is unramified at a prime <MATH_0004>\nif there exists a <MATH_0005>, <MATH_0006> such that\n<MATH_0007> is an unramified ring map. It is shown in\nAlgebra, Lemmas <REF_0002> and\n<REF_0003> that given a ring\nmap <MATH_0008> of finite type, and a prime <MATH_0009> of <MATH_0010>\nlying over <MATH_0011>, then we have\n<MATHSEG_0001> is unramified at <MATHSEG_0002> and <MATHSEG_0003> finite separable<MATHSEG_0004>\nThus we see that for a local homomorphism of local rings the properties\nof our definition above are closely related to the question of\nbeing unramified. In fact, we have proved the following lemma.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:21f9d611574416223c56ba25ea1536155c3c90b40b8feaba7d11e2e2d9e4f63e", "unit_id": "tag:024L:prose-0002"}
